That error suggests the port flag got parsed oddly. Let's do this cleanly — first let's just kill whatever's sitting on port 8501 so you can use the normal command:

bash
lsof -ti:8501 | xargs kill -9
Then run:

bash
python -m streamlit run app.py
If that still says "Port 8501 is not available" afterward, use a different port with = (safer syntax, avoids the parsing issue you just hit):

bash
python -m streamlit run app.py --server.port=8502
Then open http://localhost:8502 in your browser.

