listen the folder that i gave u at the strt was the agents correct?

Yes — the zip you uploaded (BSDI_Agentic_AI.zip) had real, working agent code in it, not just scaffolding. Specifically:

src/agents/ — this is the Track C multi-agent review board: finance_agent.py, delivery_agent.py, equity_agent.py (three specialists that independently evaluate the portfolio), plus coordinator_agent.py which merges their findings and produces the funding shortlist.
src/graph/ — this is where the actual agent loops live for Track A and B: track_a.py (plan → call a tool → look at result → answer) and track_b.py (plan which audit checks to run → run them → rank findings → report). These use LangGraph to let the LLM decide which tool to call each step, not a hardcoded sequence.
src/tools/ — the functions the agents are allowed to call (query_projects, filter_projects, the 5 audit checks, etc.).
I tested all of this directly (without even needing the UI) back when I first went through the zip — Track A answered all 4 required example questions correctly, Track B's 5 audit checks all ran and returned real counts, and Track C's coordinator produced a ranked shortlist with trade-offs. So yes: that folder was genuinely the agents, already built and functioning — what's been broken since then has been environment/dependency issues (venv, altair version, port conflicts), not the agent logic itself.

