do i need docker?

No — not for what you're doing right now. You've already got it running locally with a plain venv, and that's all you need for development, testing, and even your assignment submission.

Docker only matters if/when you want to deploy this on a server later (the "deploy live on server" part you mentioned way back at the start). At that point it's optional too — you could instead just install Python + Ollama directly on the server and run it the same way you're running it locally now (the README covers that as "Option B — systemd, no Docker").

Docker's advantage for deployment is just convenience: one command (docker compose up) spins up both the app and Ollama together, and it avoids "works on my machine" dependency issues. But it's not required — plain venv + systemd works fine too.

For now: ignore the Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml entirely. Just keep using your venv.

