should i add the track a to my original tracka file?

Yes — replace your original src/graph/track_a.py entirely with the one I gave you. Don't try to merge them by hand.

Here's why it matters: the new app.py imports a function called run_track_a_traced from that file (this is what powers the "Agent reasoning" panel showing the tool calls). Your original track_a.py doesn't have that function — only the old run_track_a. If you keep your original file, the app will crash with an ImportError as soon as you open the Data Assistant page.

To be clear on what changed in that file: I kept all your original logic (the LLM setup, the tools, the graph) exactly as it was — I just added tracing so the UI can show which tool was called and what it returned, plus made the Ollama connection configurable via an environment variable instead of hardcoded to localhost. Nothing about how the agent decides what to do was touched.

Same applies to track_b.py — replace that one too, since app.py imports run_track_b_detailed from it, which also doesn't exist in your original.







